\newlabel{fig:consumer-all-delays}{{2}{18}{A whisker plot showing the fitted model on consumer cases. The plot A is fitted on all 26 cases and it highlights those that were statistically significantly lower than 0. The plot B then fits the model with only the four cases concerning non-pecuniary damages for consumer transport. None of the cases significantly differs from 0}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces A whisker plot showing the fitted model on only the good morals and long distance contract consumer cases. Plot A contains the consumer cases with the delay decisions being excluded. Plot B is fitted on the 7 good morals cases and it highlights. We couldn't discern any interpretable trend. Plot C then fits the model with only the two cases concerning long distance contract consumer cases. None of the cases significantly differs from 0.}}{19}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:consumer-ldgm}{{3}{19}{A whisker plot showing the fitted model on only the good morals and long distance contract consumer cases. Plot A contains the consumer cases with the delay decisions being excluded. Plot B is fitted on the 7 good morals cases and it highlights. We couldn't discern any interpretable trend. Plot C then fits the model with only the two cases concerning long distance contract consumer cases. None of the cases significantly differs from 0}{figure.3}{}}
